A Mind Map for Mobile App Design in Figma can look like this:
=============================================================
                          MOBILE APP DESIGN
                                  │
 ┌────────────────────────────────┼────────────────────────────────┐
 │                                │                                │
User Research              Information Architecture         Visual Design
 │                                │                                │
 ├─ Target Users                ├─ App Structure              ├─ Color Palette
 ├─ Personas                    ├─ User Flow                  ├─ Typography
 ├─ User Needs                  ├─ Navigation                 ├─ Icons
 └─ User Goals                  └─ Screen Hierarchy           └─ Design System
                                  │
                                  │
                             Wireframing
                                  │
                 ├─ Splash Screen
                 ├─ Login / Signup
                 ├─ Home Screen
                 ├─ Profile Screen
                 ├─ Settings Screen
                 └─ Navigation Bar
                                  │
                                  │
                              Prototyping
                                  │
                 ├─ Screen Transitions
                 ├─ Gestures
                 ├─ Animations
                 ├─ Interactive Elements
                 └─ User Journey
                                  │
                                  │
                           Usability Testing
                                  │
                 ├─ User Feedback
                 ├─ Accessibility Check
                 ├─ Error Identification
                 └─ Design Improvements
                                  │
                                  │
                           Developer Handoff
                                  │
                 ├─ Components
                 ├─ Assets Export
                 ├─ Design Specifications
                 └─ Documentation

FigJam Layout Example
======================
                         [Mobile App Design]
                                  │
      ┌────────────┬────────────┬────────────┬────────────┐
      │            │            │            │
  Research        IA       Wireframes    Visual Design
      │            │            │            │
  Personas     User Flow   Home Screen   Colors
  Goals        Navigation  Login Screen  Typography
  Needs        Structure   Profile       Icons
                                  │
                            Prototyping
                                  │
                      Gestures • Animation
                                  │
                             Testing
                                  │
                     Feedback • Accessibility
                                  │
                        Developer Handoff
                                  │
                    Components • Assets • Specs

For most mobile app projects in Figma, the design flow is:
=========================================================
Research → Personas → User Flow → Wireframes → Visual Design → Prototype → Testing → Developer 
Handoff.

NOTE:
=====
You can create mind maps in both Figma and FigJam, but FigJam is the better tool for mind mapping.
